  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46232\", \"PowerToys#48211\"], \"answer\": \"This request has been filed before. PowerToys#46232 ('Allow all system tray icons to be displayed on the dock') is the tracking thread, and PowerToys#48211 points to it for the tray part of its request. The PowerToys team said they probably can't ship tray-icon support in the Dock themselves. They left the thread open as a tracker and said they would welcome a third-party Command Palette extension that shows tray icons as a dock band. Add a thumbs-up to #46232 rather than opening a new request. For now, keep using the Windows taskbar's notification area for background apps. A community-built dock band extension is the likely route if you want this sooner.\"}",
